---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import AppShell from '@/layouts/AppShell.astro';
---

<Base lang="en">
  <AppShell>
    <main id="intro" slot="fallback">
      <div>
        <h1>Fahsai — Thailand Air Quality Map</h1>
        <p>
          Fahsai (<span lang="th">ฟ้าใส</span>, “clear sky”) is a free, non-commercial map of the
          causes of seasonal air pollution in Thailand and its neighbours. It shows satellite fire
          detections, PM2.5 readings from ground stations, gridded PM2.5 estimates, wind patterns
          and power plants on one map, updated daily.
        </p>
        <p>
          It covers Thailand, Myanmar, Laos, Cambodia, Vietnam and Singapore, with up to 120 days
          of history, so you can see how fires, wind and air quality change together through the
          haze season.
        </p>
        <p>Loading the map… If it doesn’t appear, try reloading the page.</p>
        <noscript><p>The map needs JavaScript.</p></noscript>
        <h2>Data sources</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Fire data courtesy NASA FIRMS (<a href="https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov"
              >firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov</a
            >)
          </li>
          <li>Air quality data from OpenAQ (<a href="https://openaq.org">openaq.org</a>)</li>
          <li>
            <a href="https://open-meteo.com/">Weather data by Open-Meteo.com</a> (CC BY 4.0)
          </li>
          <li>
            Power plant data from WRI Global Power Plant Database (<a
              href="https://resourcewatch.org"
              >resourcewatch.org</a
            >) (CC BY 4.0)
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p><a href="/th/" lang="th" hreflang="th">ภาษาไทย</a></p>
      </div>
    </main>
  </AppShell>
</Base>
